# Commits that only change layout, which `git blame` should look past to
# the commit that last changed what a line does. GitHub's blame view reads
# this file by itself. A local git needs telling, once per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full SHA per line, as it landed on main, so a squash merge's entry
# can only be written after that merge. Each entry names its PR above it.

# #953: `ruff format` over every script under scripts/ (#938). It also carried
# a few real lines in scripts/self-tests.sh, scripts/lint.sh and ruff.toml,
# which this hides too. `git blame --ignore-revs-file= <file>` shows them.
